speechtext:
For a copy of all orders in council, regulations, directions, correspondence and all other documents passed between the government or any minister or department of the government and the Saddle Lake Indian Band, or the Soldier Settlement Board, or the Indian agent of the said reserve or any person or (persons, or between the said Soldier Settlement Board or the said Indian agent and any person or persons relating to or in connection with the surrender or sale of any portion of the Saddle Lake reserve during the years 1925 and 1926, including the conditions of such sale and all reports made thereon and including also the names, addresses and occupations of,
(a)	The applicants for purchase;
(b)	The applicants who balloted for the right to purchase;
Boundary Waters Treaty

(c)	The successful purchasers or allottees with the number of acres purchased by or alloted to each;
(d) The names and addresses of such of the said successful purchasers or allottees as were at the date of the said sale bona fide farmers, and the acreage then being actually farmed by each;
(e)	The names and addresses of such of said last-mentioned persons as carried on any other profession or business in addition to farming, and the description of such additional occupation.
